 eat cheese, olives, tomatoes and bread.":"r","My brother always drinks milk, but I prefer tea.":"r","My school is not far from our house, so I walk there with my best friend, Deniz.":"r","We talk and laugh on the way.":"r","Classes start at half past eight.":"r","On Saturdays, I don't get up early.":"r","I sleep until ten and have a big breakfast with my grandparents.":"r","Every Saturday morning, Ali goes to the market with his grandmother.":"r","The market is near their house, and it is always busy and noisy.":"r","His grandmother has a shopping list.":"r","This week they need potatoes, onions, apples and some fresh fish.":"r","Ali carries the bags because his grandmother's bags are heavy.":"r","The fruit seller is a friendly man.":"r","He gives Ali a free orange every week.":"r","\"You are a good helper,\" he says.":"r","The fish is expensive today, so they buy chicken instead.":"r","On the way home, they stop at a small café.":"r","His grandmother drinks Turkish coffee and Ali has a lemonade.":"r","Ali loves Saturdays.":"r","Last month, a new family moved into the flat next to ours.":"r","They are from Canada.":"r","The father, Tom, is an English teacher at a university in Ankara.":"r","Tom has two children, Lily and Jack.":"r","Lily is ten and Jack is seven.":"r","They don't speak much Turkish yet, but they are learning quickly.":"r","Yesterday, my mother made a cake and we took it to their flat.":"r","Tom was very happy.":"r","He said, \"Thank you so much!":"r","In Canada, we do the same thing for new neighbors.\"":"r","Now Lily and I play together after school.":"r","I help her with Turkish, and she helps me with English.":"r","It's a good deal for both of us!":"r","On Sunday, my family wanted to have a picnic in the park.":"r","We prepared sandwiches, fruit and lemonade.":"r","But when we opened the door, it was raining heavily.":"r","\"Oh no!":"r","What can we do now?\"":"r","asked my sister.":"r","My father had an idea.":"r","\"Let's have a picnic in the living room!\"":"r","We put a big blanket on the floor and sat on it.":"r","We ate our sandwiches and played board games all afternoon.":"r","My mother won every game, and we laughed a lot.":"r","In the evening, the rain stopped and we saw a beautiful rainbow from the window.":"r","It was not the day we planned, but it was a really fun day.":"r","When Mert started university in another city, he had a big problem: he couldn't cook.":"r","For the first few weeks, he ate fast food almost every day.":"r","He soon felt tired, and he was spending too much money.":"r","One evening, he decided to watch a cooking video online.":"r","The recipe was simple: lentil soup.":"r","He followed the steps carefully, and to his surprise, the soup tasted just like his mother's.":"r","After that, Mert watched a new video every few days.":"r","He learned how to make pasta, rice and even a few desserts.":"r","He also started a notebook where he wrote down his favorite recipes and the mistakes he made.":"r","Now his flatmates often ask him to cook for them.":"r","\"I'm not a chef,\" Mert says, \"but I've learned that cooking is just like any other skill.":"r","You get better with practice.\"":"r","Many parents complain that their teenage children stay up late and are hard to wake up in the morning.":"r","They often think this is just laziness, but scientists say there is a biological reason.":"r","During the teenage years, the body releases the sleep hormone, melatonin, later in the evening than it does in children or adults.":"r","As a result, most teenagers don't feel sleepy until around eleven o'clock at night.":"r","Experts recommend that teenagers sleep between eight and ten hours a night.":"r","However, because school starts early, many of them sleep only six or seven hours.":"r","This lack of sleep can affect their mood, their memory and their grades.":"r","Some schools have started classes later in the morning.":"r","In these schools, students arrive less tired, and their test results have improved.":"r","Doctors also advise teenagers to put their phones away an hour before bed, because the light from screens makes it even harder to fall asleep.":"r","Last summer, Sarah, a nurse from Manchester, finally made her dream come true: a hot-air balloon ride in Cappadocia.":"r","She had to get up at four in the morning because the balloons take off before sunrise, when the air is calm.":"r","A small bus picked her up from her hotel and took her to a large field.":"r","There, dozens of colorful balloons were slowly filling with hot air.":"r","\"At first I was a bit nervous,\" Sarah admits, \"but as soon as we rose into the sky, I forgot all my fears.\"":"r","From above, she could see the famous fairy chimneys, the valleys and the small villages.":"r","The sun came up and turned the rocks pink and gold.":"r","The flight lasted about an hour.":"r","After landing, the pilot opened a bottle of fruit juice to celebrate.":"r","Sarah says it was expensive, but worth every penny.":"r","\"If you ever visit Turkey,\" she advises, \"don't miss it.\"":"r","When people think of a library, they usually imagine quiet rooms full of old books.":"r","But modern libraries are changing fast.":"r","In many cities, libraries now lend much more than books.":"r","You can borrow laptops, cameras, musical instruments and even tools for repairing things at home.":"r","Some libraries have \"makerspaces\" with 3D printers, where young people can design and build their own projects.":"r","Libraries have also become important meeting places.":"r","They offer free language classes, help for job seekers and activities for children and older people.":"r","For many people who live alone, the library is one of the few places where they can spend time with others without paying anything.":"r","Of course, books are still at the heart of every library.":"r","But librarians say their real job is not just to look after books.":"r","\"Our job,\" one librarian explains, \"is to give everyone the same chance to learn.\"":"r","For more than a century, the five-day working week has been the norm in most countries.":"r","Recently, however, a growing number of companies have experimented with a four-day week, in which employees work fewer hours for the same salary.":"r","The results of several large trials have been surprisingly positive.":"r","In one study involving dozens of companies, most employers reported that productivity stayed the same or even increased.":"r","Employees, meanwhile, said they felt less stressed, slept better and had more time for their families and hobbies.":"r","Perhaps most importantly for businesses, fewer staff quit their jobs during the trial.":"r","Critics, though, argue that the model does not suit every sector.":"r","A hospital or a restaurant cannot simply close for an extra day, and in some jobs, squeezing five days of work into four may actually increase pressure on workers.":"r","Supporters respond that the four-day week is less about the exact number of days and more about rethinking how we work.":"r","Shorter meetings, fewer distractions and clearer priorities, they say, could benefit any workplace, whatever schedule it follows.":"r","Plastic is cheap, light and incredibly useful, which explains why the world produces hundreds of millions of tonnes of it every year.":"r","Yet the very quality that makes plastic so practical — its durability — is also what makes it a serious environmental threat.":"r","A plastic bottle can take hundreds of years to break down.":"r","Rather than disappearing, it gradually breaks into smaller and smaller pieces known as microplastics.":"r","These tiny particles have been found almost everywhere scientists have looked: in deep ocean water, in Arctic ice, and even in the food we eat and the air we breathe.":"r","Marine animals are among the most affected.":"r","Sea turtles mistake plastic bags for jellyfish, while seabirds feed plastic fragments to their chicks.":"r","Many of these animals die because their stomachs are full of material they cannot digest.":"r","Recycling helps, but only a small proportion of plastic is actually recycled.":"r","For this reason, many experts believe the most effective solution is to reduce the amount we use in the first place — for example, by choosing reusable bags and bottles, and by supporting laws that limit single-use plastics.":"r","For a long time, many parents worried that raising a child with two languages would confuse them or slow down their development.":"r","Today, most research suggests the opposite: speaking more than one language may actually offer the brain some valuable advantages.":"r","When bilingual people speak, both of their languages remain active in the brain, even if they are only using one.":"r","To avoid mixing them up, the brain constantly has to choose one language and suppress the other.":"r","Some scientists believe that this daily mental exercise strengthens skills such as attention, focus and switching quickly between tasks.":"r","There may be long-term benefits too.":"r","Several studies have found that, on average, bilingual people develop the symptoms of dementia a few years later than people who speak only one language.":"r","Researchers think that years of managing two languages may help build a kind of \"cognitive reserve\" that protects the brain as it ages.":"r","It is worth noting that not all studies agree, and the advantages may depend on how often and how well people use both languages.":"r","Nevertheless, the message for learners is encouraging: it is never too late to start, and every new word is a workout for your brain.":"r","Online learning was once seen as a second-best option, mainly for people who could not attend a real classroom.":"r","In recent years, however, it has become a normal part of education for millions of students around the world.":"r","Its advantages are clear.":"r","Students can watch lessons again as many times as they need, study at their own pace and access courses from top universities without leaving home.":"r","For people with jobs or family responsibilities, this flexibility can make the difference between studying and not studying at all.":"r","Yet online learning also has its drawbacks.":"r","Without a fixed timetable, many students find it hard to stay motivated, and a large proportion of people who sign up for free online courses never finish them.":"r","Others miss the social side of school: the conversations in the corridor, the group projects and the simple experience of learning alongside friends.":"r","Many educators now believe the future lies in a mix of both.":"r","In this \"blended\" model, students learn basic content online and use classroom time for discussion, practice and teamwork — the things that are hardest to do through a screen.":"r","It seems self-evident that having more options makes us happier.":"r","If a café offers fifty kinds of coffee rather than five, surely every customer is more likely to find exactly what they want.":"r","Yet a substantial body of research suggests that, beyond a certain point, abundant choice can leave us less satisfied rather than more.":"r","One frequently cited experiment illustrates the point.":"r","Shoppers in a supermarket were offered free samples of jam, sometimes from a table displaying twenty-four varieties and sometimes from one displaying only six.":"r","The larger display attracted more attention, but customers who saw the smaller selection were considerably more likely to actually buy a jar.":"r","Psychologists offer several explanations.":"r","Evaluating dozens of alternatives is mentally exhausting, so we may postpone the decision altogether.":"r","And once we do choose, the sheer number of rejected options makes it easier to imagine that one of them would have been better, leaving us with a lingering sense of regret.":"r","None of this means that choice is undesirable; being able to choose is fundamental to our sense of autonomy.":"r","The lesson, perhaps, is that we should be more deliberate about which decisions really deserve our time — and allow ourselves to settle for \"good enough\" in the rest.":"r","On a hot summer afternoon, the centre of a large city can be several degrees warmer than the countryside just a few kilometres away.":"r","This phenomenon, known as the urban heat island effect, is becoming an increasingly pressing concern as heatwaves grow more frequent and intense.":"r","The causes are largely a consequence of how cities are built.":"r","Dark surfaces such as asphalt and roofing absorb sunlight during the day and release it slowly at night, preventing the city from cooling down.":"r","Dense buildings obstruct the wind, while air conditioners, vehicles and factories pump additional heat into the streets.":"r","Crucially, cities often lack the vegetation that, in rural areas, cools the air through shade and evaporation.":"r","The consequences are not merely a matter of discomfort.":"r","Extreme urban heat has been linked to higher rates of illness and death, particularly among elderly people and those living in poorly insulated housing, and it drives up energy demand as residents turn to air conditioning.":"r","Fortunately, the remedies are well understood.":"r","Planting trees, creating parks, installing \"green roofs\" and painting surfaces in lighter colours can all significantly reduce local temperatures.":"r","The challenge lies less in knowing what to do than in persuading cities to invest before the next heatwave arrives.":"r","Not long ago, creativity was widely regarded as the one domain in which humans would remain unchallenged by machines.":"r","Computers might beat us at chess or calculate faster than any mathematician, the argument went, but they could never write a poem, compose a melody or paint a picture worth looking at.":"r","That assumption has been seriously shaken.":"r","Today's artificial intelligence systems can generate essays, images and music in seconds, and their output is sometimes difficult to distinguish from human work.":"r","Some artists have embraced these tools as a new kind of brush; others regard them as a threat to their livelihoods and to the very idea of art.":"r","The debate often hinges on what we mean by creativity.":"r","If it simply means producing something new and valuable, then machines arguably already qualify.":"r","But many philosophers insist that genuine creativity involves intention, experience and the desire to communicate something — qualities that current systems, which work by identifying patterns in vast amounts of existing data, do not appear to possess.":"r","Perhaps the more productive question is not whether machines can be creative, but how they will change human creativity.":"r","Just as photography did not end painting but pushed it in new directions, AI may ultimately prompt us to reconsider what is uniquely valuable about the things we make.":"r","Few of us willingly spend time doing nothing.":"r","The moment we find ourselves waiting for a bus or standing in a queue, most of us instinctively reach for our phones.":"r","Boredom, it seems, has become something to be eliminated at all costs.":"r","Yet a growing number of psychologists argue that this may come at a price.":"r","Boredom, they suggest, is not simply an unpleasant emotion but a useful signal: it tells us that our current situation is not meeting our needs and nudges us to seek something more meaningful.":"r","When we immediately silence that signal with endless scrolling, we may lose the motivation to change direction.":"r","There is also evidence that boredom can fuel creativity.":"r","In one study, participants who first completed a deliberately dull task — copying numbers from a phone book — subsequently came up with more inventive ideas than those who had not.":"r","Researchers believe that when the mind is under-stimulated, it begins to wander, making unexpected connections between ideas.":"r","This is not an argument for seeking out tedium, nor for abandoning technology.":"r","It is, rather, an invitation to tolerate the occasional empty moment.":"r","The next time you feel bored, consider leaving your phone in your pocket for a few minutes.":"r","You may be surprised where your thoughts take you.":"r","furniture":"w","We bought new furniture for the living room.":"s","drawer":"w","The keys are in the top drawer.":"s","shelf":"w","Put the books back on the shelf, please.":"s","fridge":"w","There's some milk in the fridge.":"s","rent":"w","The rent is due at the beginning of the month.":"s","landlord":"w","Our landlord fixed the heating yesterday.":"s","tidy":"w","Her room is always clean and tidy.":"s","mess":"w","Sorry about the mess — I'm moving house.":"s","Can I borrow your umbrella?":"s","plug in":"w","Don't forget to plug in your phone.":"s","cosy":"w","It's a small but very cosy flat.":"s","upstairs":"w","The bathroom is upstairs, on the left.":"s","subject":"w","Maths is my favourite subject.":"s","homework":"w","I haven't finished my homework yet.":"s","pass":"w","I hope I pass the exam tomorrow.":"s","fail":"w","He failed his driving test twice.":"s","revise":"w","I need to revise for my history exam.":"s","grade":"w","She got the highest grade in the class.":"s","The new term starts in September.":"s","degree":"w","She has a degree in engineering.":"s","scholarship":"w","He won a scholarship to study in Germany.":"s","attend":"w","All students must attend the meeting.":"s","essay":"w","We have to write an essay about climate change.":"s","take notes":"w","Try to take notes during the lecture.":"s","price":"w","The price of bread has gone up again.":"s","discount":"w","Students get a 10% discount.":"s","receipt":"w","Keep the receipt in case you want to return it.":"s","refund":"w","I took the shoes back and got a refund.":"s","afford":"w","We can't afford a new car this year.":"s","cash":"w","Do you accept cash or only cards?":"s","change":"w","Here's your change, sir.":"s","try on":"w","Can I try on this jacket?":"s","bargain":"w","This coat was a real bargain.":"s","save":"w","I'm saving money for a holiday.":"s","spend":"w","How much did you spend on clothes?":"s","out of stock":"w","Sorry, that size is out of stock.":"s","crossroads":"w","Turn left at the crossroads.":"s","pedestrian":"w","This street is only for pedestrians.":"s","traffic jam":"w","We were stuck in a traffic jam for an hour.":"s","stop":"w","Get off at the next stop.":"s","miss":"w","Hurry up or we'll miss the bus!":"s","crowded":"w","The metro is very crowded in the morning.":"s","get lost":"w","We got lost in the old part of the city.":"s","directions":"w","Could you give me directions to the station?":"s","nearby":"w","Is there a pharmacy nearby?":"s","rush hour":"w","Avoid driving during rush hour.":"s","park":"w","You can't park here; it's a bus lane.":"s","downtown":"w","Let's meet downtown after work.":"s","team":"w","Which team do you support?":"s","match":"w","Did you watch the match last night?":"s","win":"w","Our team won 3–1.":"s","lose":"w","I hate losing at board games.":"s","score":"w","He scored in the last minute.":"s","coach":"w","Our coach is very strict but fair.":"s","work out":"w","I work out three times a week.":"s","hobby":"w","Painting is a relaxing hobby.":"s","take up":"w","I've taken up yoga this year.":"s","be into":"w","She's really into photography.":"s","competition":"w","He entered a chess competition.":"s","spare time":"w","What do you do in your spare time?":"s","headline":"w","The story made the headlines around the world.":"s","source":"w","Always check the source of the news.":"s","fake news":"w","Fake news spreads faster than the truth.":"s","post":"w","She posted a photo of her new puppy.":"s","follower":"w","The account has over a million followers.":"s","go viral":"w","His video went viral overnight.":"s","broadcast":"w","The final will be broadcast live.":"s","advertisement":"w","I skip every advertisement on YouTube.":"s","In my opinion, the film was too long.":"s","misleading":"w","The title of the article is very misleading.":"s","subscribe":"w","Subscribe to our newsletter for updates.":"s","journalist":"w","The journalist interviewed the mayor.":"s","More research is needed on this topic.":"s","evidence":"w","There is no evidence that the drug works.":"s","hypothesis":"w","The experiment supported their hypothesis.":"s","experiment":"w","They carried out an experiment on mice.":"s","findings":"w","The findings were published in a journal.":"s","significant":"w","There was a significant drop in temperature.":"s","conduct":"w","The survey was conducted online.":"s","analyse":"w","Scientists are analysing the data.":"s","breakthrough":"w","The vaccine was a medical breakthrough.":"s","theory":"w","Darwin's theory changed biology forever.":"s","peer review":"w","The paper is still under peer review.":"s","inconclusive":"w","The results of the study were inconclusive.":"s"}